onse to DNA damage</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>7644</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10618704</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.onc.1203015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ichijo</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>From receptors to stress-activated MAP kinases</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>6087</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10557099</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.onc.1203129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Basu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolesnick</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stress signals for apoptosis: ceramide and c-Jun kinase</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>3277</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><comment>1998 Dec 24</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9916990</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.onc.1202570</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holbrook</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Fornace</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Signaling events controlling the molecular response to genotoxic stress</article-title><source>EXS</source><year>1996</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>273</fpage><lpage>88</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8856980</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bulavin</surname><given-names>DV</given-names></name><name><surname>Amundson</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Fornace</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>p38 and Chk1 kinases: different conductors for the G(2)/M checkpoint symphony</article-title><source>Curr Opin Genet Dev</source><year>2002</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>92</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11790561</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0959-437X(01)00270-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abdollahi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffman-Liebermann</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Liebermann</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sequence and expression of a cDNA encoding MyD118: A novel myeloid differentiation primary response gene induced by multiple cytokines</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1991</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>167</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1899477</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Bae</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Krishnaraju</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Azam</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Fan</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffman</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Liebermann</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CR6: A third member in the MyD118 &#x00026; Gadd 45 gene family which functions in negative growth control</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>1999</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>4899</fpage><lpage>4907</lpage><pub-